{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418390-exalted-written-campaign","id":1418390,"title":"Exalted Written Campaign","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-15T10:12:41-07:00","id":1418390,"title":"Exalted Written Campaign","content":"I\u2019ve been thinking about writing an entire Exalted campaign, although maybe a short one, like something that takes 10+ sessions to get through. I\u2019m not quite sure on the best way to do it. I\u2019ll start with some hurdles that I don\u2019t think I need help with.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think I need help with the Exalted problem of players just having too much power and wrecking any campaign you might have. Sure they have a lot of power, but you can make campaigns for high level DnD characters that can teleport across the universe, decimate armies with a single spell, divine impossible to know information, and just straight up wish for things to happen and then they do. It still works you just need to take that into account. Sure the players could just right angle and leave the whole thing, but that\u2019s true of any kind of published adventure in any game. I\u2019ll find a way to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Where I need some help is how do I present different varied difficult tasks, and looking for suggestions on what people might want to see it be about.<br /> <br /> For example I know with the way characters can vastly differ in optimization that many of the scenes are going to have to have basically a difficulty slider. How would it be best to present that? I\u2019d like to keep one setting as a kind of default to make reading it flow easier, but what setting is the default, hard or easy? I don\u2019t want people thinking their bad at the game for having to turn on easy mode, but I also don\u2019t want STs to feel like they\u2019re being unfair turning on hard mode.<br /> <br /> Another thing is how wide should that gulf be? Should I even attempt to write for a group of hyper-optimized characters? Or should I just ditch that and write for more what the system expects? Maybe I should include a sample circle or guidelines for what the campaign expects?<br /> <br /> Also taking suggestions for what it\u2019s about. Adventure on the high seas squaring off against an undead captain/fleet. Deep investigators solving crimes in the big city? Tomb raiders exploring a series of ancient ruins? Battling cults and the forces of Hell in the frozen northern wastes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T12:22:38-07:00","id":1418401,"title":"","content":"Maybe write with the default expectation of an Exalt having 7-10 dots and 2-3 Charms? That's a fair estimation of a secondary specialist or a low-op build, to which you could add modifications for &quot;what if this is someone's Supernal?&quot; and &quot;what if no-one really invested in this?&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel like the more important part will be in how you structure the challenges, rather than the difficulty of any one scene. If the circle is going to have to fight off a legion of hungry ghosts, descend a thousand-mile deep cave, and persuade a god of death to leave their village alone, it won't matter so much if one or two challenges get trivialized--something else will wind up being an obstacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T12:23:10-07:00","id":1418402,"title":"","content":"I'd actually recommend three settings. Unoptimized starting characters, mostly optimized starting characters (assume 5s in dex and at least one combat/defensive ability), and experienced/really well optimized characters. In my experience, most players end up at the second one, unless your ST pushed them pretty firmly towards one of the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T12:56:03-07:00","id":1418405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418390-exalted-written-campaign?p=1418401#post1418401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe write with the default expectation of an Exalt having 7-10 dots and 2-3 Charms? That's a fair estimation of a secondary specialist or a low-op build, to which you could add modifications for &amp;quot;what if this is someone's Supernal?&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;what if no-one really invested in this?&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that might be a good assumption. I also expect most challenged to become trivialized, I just also expect to make PCs pay for it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scrollreader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418390-exalted-written-campaign?p=1418402#post1418402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd actually recommend three settings. Unoptimized starting characters, mostly optimized starting characters (assume 5s in dex and at least one combat/defensive ability), and experienced/really well optimized characters. In my experience, most players end up at the second one, unless your ST pushed them pretty firmly towards one of the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making scenes with 3 might be more work than I am willing to do, especially if for one of those I have to try and find ways to make broken optimized characters work for it. Especially since the gulf between the highest and lowest is so massive. I\u2019d have to go from fighting bandits to fighting Alhat and his entire pantheon of war gods, which would make the flow a lot harder to maintain.<br /> <br /> I just don\u2019t know if more people play unoptimized characters than play hyper optimized ones. Also for hyper optimized I\u2019m not just talking about combat, if you have max dex and Melee, but heavy armor, no dodge, resistance, stamina, Athletics or integrity you\u2019ll be hurting anyway. Somebody who has dex 5, but heavy armor and doge zero is getting hammered by an avalanche of rocks or something at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T14:16:30-07:00","id":1418412,"title":"","content":"Actually, hyper optimized might be misleading. I can do okay designing encounters with one character who\u2019s super combat optimized, but not if the whole team is, but that\u2019s also different from being really optimized in your focus.<br /> <br /> Like a whole party can have 5s in dex and Melee with a specialty and 3 combat charms and already that\u2019s nearly impossible to deal with. Maybe fin include enough other stuff it won\u2019t matter though? So they kill that combat encounter in literally less than one round, but then let\u2019s do 5 non-combat scenes that don\u2019t involve combat stats at all and are actually worth bringing out the dice for. <br /> <br /> Then on the other side of that though is all the fighting parts are boring for anyone who actually wants to do fights stuff.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve had it before that failing non-combat encounters somehow strengthens the combat one later, but that\u2019s a hard gimmick to constantly keep up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T23:13:55-07:00","id":1418484,"title":"","content":"What if there were multiple routes or optional areas? That might make things a lot easier to write. Rather than have alternate versions for scenes, have optional scenes to insert to ratchet things up. I might be able to do that without it becoming artificial feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T23:56:03-07:00","id":1418488,"title":"","content":"I think you are over-thinking it.<br /> <br /> Write the campaign you want to write, and include session 0 guidance for the types of character your campaign is geared for.<br /> <br /> If an ST wants to allow different types of characters, then it's on them to modify the campaign accordingly.<br /> <br /> (In other words, write it in Easy Mode and tell the PCs &quot;no, you can't have Dex 5, Melee 5, Sword Specialty, 6 Melee Charms and a Daiklave on your Twilight&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T07:28:19-07:00","id":1418525,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that\u2019s a good point. Plus that way I can include things that suggest what kind of characters to being. That way nobody is fielding their sail supernal in the deep underground caverns of the jadeborn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T05:02:01-07:00","id":1418652,"title":"","content":"I honestly think you're asking for something impossible. Anything beyond &quot;here are some principal characters, their goals, flaws, and abilities, Enter Sandbox&quot; is doomed to failure. <br /> <br /> Think of a game with really good quests, like New Vegas or Witcher 3, and think about all the work put in to making different options available to you. In New Vegas you could conceivably have a skill rank 100 in Stealth, Lockpicking, Science (Hacking), Repair, or Medicine, and a Perk on top of that, which means if that option exists than you find it and succeed at your strong suit. The problem with Exalted is that you can reasonably expect a player be <i>the best person in the world at their strong suit</i>. Combat aside, I've never felt challenged in my specialty in Exalted. You're just too damn good unless its a head to head with other Exalted designed to oppose you. In Witcher 3 you don't really have any skills besides Use Sword On Monster and its twin sister Use Sword On Man with their two cousins Highlight Plot Point and Jedi Mind Trick, so in that game all quests are really decided by characterization and choice, deciding who lives and dies, and dealing with the consequences of that decision. That kind of quest lives and dies in the ST's ability to roleplay NPCs and the player's level of engagement. Its probably the easiest thing to fuck up. <br /> <br /> So if you want to design a <i><b>ten session</b></i> adventure, you basically have to give me a broad strokes only coloring book picture and let me paint in <i><b>everything else</b></i>. Solar Exalted all have the same power, and that's access to the Supernal Ability called Breaking The Game, and there's just no way to account for that. You'd have better luck giving us a handful of scenarios and colorful NPCs and letting the ST change things to fit the table. DnD adventures work because player abilities are tightly controlled and even then, players still screw everything up. Just google a reddit thread about Waterdeep Dragon Heist to see what I mean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-17T23:42:08-07:00","id":1418777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418390-exalted-written-campaign?p=1418652#post1418652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if you want to design a <i><b>ten session</b></i> adventure, you basically have to give me a broad strokes only coloring book picture and let me paint in <i><b>everything else</b></i>. Solar Exalted all have the same power, and that's access to the Supernal Ability called Breaking The Game, and there's just no way to account for that. You'd have better luck giving us a handful of scenarios and colorful NPCs and letting the ST change things to fit the table. DnD adventures work because player abilities are tightly controlled and even then, players still screw everything up. Just google a reddit thread about Waterdeep Dragon Heist to see what I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Respectfully I disagree. I don't think any adventure can claim to be immune to players breaking it in one way or another, in any system. I've done Dragonheist, Dungeon of the Mad Mage, Icewind Dale and a few more and they've all gone absolutely butter smooth for me. Dragonheist isn't even that well written, there's no heist!<br /> <br /> Either way, there's strategies to help control the narrative flow. Having events take place in a sequence, events that take place when the players aren't there, controlling information that the players have, etc. For example, let me lay one out<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Session 1</b><br /> The players are in a satrapy and at a big social function they learn, one way or another, that there may be a rash of missing children cases showing up in the city. An investigation reveals it's not just children, although the adults going missing are mostly people that society ignores. Furthermore some information leads them to believe the missing people are being taken to a location a day's travel out of town. Something more is off though, the last people they got that info from were definitely more badass than your typical mortal kidnappers.<br /> <br /> <b>Session 2</b><br /> The location however is again suspiciously difficult to find, clearly being hidden by magic, and the surrounding area has animals or animalistic spirits far more dangerous than one would expect of that area. Either somebody did that intentionally, or something else has them riled up. The location they find though is just a temporary stopover, to another place where they are &quot;processed&quot; The final person here is also supernaturally gifted, maybe an Exalt of some kind, and attempts to convince the players that what he's doing is not wrong.<br /> <br /> <b>Session 3</b><br /> This place is nearby, again maybe a day's travel. This time though, the place isn't just in an area with riled up unnaturally dangerous shit, it's clearly wrong in some very serious ways. Just the trek to get there leads through a tangle of venomous barbed plants, crawling with legendarily massive predatory insects. Inside it's even even stranger, and the first evidence of what's truly happening here appears as creatures from the Wyld are among the defenders. They rescue the most recent captures, but find that the rest have been long gone to their lord to be dream eaten or worse.<br /> <br /> <b>Session 4</b><br /> The group is large, dozens of people at least, and leaving them to return home on their own through the Wyld tainted forest is a death sentence, they must be escorted back or die. The trip however, reveals just how deep this corruption goes, encountering many dangers that are made all the more difficult because of the people the heroes are trying to protect. The last of these dangers is a Raksha hunting party. That party comes with the information that this is no mere storm of chaos blowing in from Creation's edge, but a crusade. An ancient fey with a grudge against this area of Creation has come to claim it and fill it with chaos. He's already retaken the old capital and is using it as his headquarters.<br /> <br /> <b>Session 5</b><br /> Either through the player's lore knowledge or possibly allies in the city they find that the location of this old capital have been expunged from the records, even Exalted scholars who've tried to search for them have been unable to find even the records of where to start looking. Likely unbeknownst to the players this expunging of info was carried out by Sidereal Exalted, masters of the craft. There are very few people who even know where to look for the information, and they hold their secrets tightly.<br /> <br /> Also the surrounding countryside is being ravaged by the Fey. All over for a hundred miles it seems people are being taken and killed, and monsters roam freely.<br /> <br /> <b>Session 6</b><br /> The people, or maybe even person, who knows where the info might be is an exalted socialite who's holding a grand party, it might be the end of the world after all so let's get it on. The information simply doesn't exist anywhere except inside her head, and they have to get there and convince her to give it up. Of course this isn't as easy as just walking in the front door and asking her, for various reasons.<br /> <br /> <b>Session 7</b><br /> The players are successful, they find that information, and indeed, do find the information. The city was sent from its location in the valley, deep below a mountain by some incredible magic (Neighborhood Relocation) and it's from there that this fairy king commands attacks on the land. He's the only one that can stop them, or at least his death will kill his crusade's momentum. Also he has likely taken this ancient city and warped it into a truly truly epic fortress. Not only equipped with ancient defense mechanisms, but the structures have been warped by chaos and filled with terrors. Still the heroes succeed and kill him. Unfortunately he has one last spiteful stab of fury, captain Ahab style.<br /> <br /> <b>Session 8</b><br /> As the Wyld Storm begins to break, its final stages are the most dangerous, and the city is besieged by nightmares. The land heaves, buildings walk, and through it all the heroes make a last desperate stand to mitigate the untold damage and prevent the city form being torn apart. After which the storm subsides, and if they're anathema, they now have to deal with revealing that to a devoutly immaculate population if at any point in this adventure they displayed their power. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's only 8 sessions because I want to leave room for players to roleplay more, or do their own side things if they feel they have the time. Also I came up with it in like 30 mintues.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That sounds like it could be a pretty good outline, and I'm struggling to think of a Supernal that turns that into a complete joke, especially if you really vary up the stuff and keep the pressure high. There's no Essence 5 Lore or Investigation charm that just lets you instantly know that this missing persons case is actually connected to a massive fairy crusade, and also where the King is, so you can go Dawn him in the face in one session.<br /> <br /> I can definitely see that this chain of events might go off the rails if the whole party is just like &quot;Fuck missing people, mortals are worthless, let's get out of this place&quot; but you really need to expect at least a certain amount of player buy-in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T06:06:38-07:00","id":1418996,"title":"","content":"I like it, it's a good overview. I'd be happy to play this adventure. But until the actual specifics come out I can't say whether or not various supernals break the game. <br /> <br /> I mean, unless a Solar Diplomat convinces the Big Bad to call of the attack. But they need to meet a Solar Socialite first which is difficult, unless a Stealth or Larcenist sneak in to her room. Or a Socialize, Presence, Performance supernal charm their way right through the front door. And of course, you planned for a party that can fly to skip the Difficult Travel problems of Session 2, 3, 4, and possibly 7. <br /> <br /> Session 5 has the opposite problem: it seems to be a wyld goose chase, the Solars cant find the information at all, in any way, no matter what. I hope the Investigate Supernal is ok with that. Considering that half of the high end charms are &quot;do the recreate the crime scene in lerfect detail thing from Sherlock&quot; and Evidence Restoring Prana exists, I'd personally feel cheated about all of that. Even if that leads to the Socialite, getting no-sold on your specialty sucks.<br /> <br /> Again, this is still the outline. You're going to have to write every single piece of this adventure under the caveat that its possible and more than likely probable that players will completely bypass each step. You need to plan for what happens when a Social/Presence/Performance Supernal uses Solar Mind Control on the npcs. You need to plan for Travel Without Distance, Airships, Nimbus Cloud, Storm Wind Rider, Essence Gliders, and Wings. What if the party has a Fair Folk on their team? My circle has two. Do they know about this attack? Did you consider that a player even has them? They boss from Session 2, do they know where the big bad is? What if the players convince him to switch sides and they jump right to session 6? How much does Order Affirming Blow and Wyld Shaping Technique affect the final battle? Oh, and why isnt the Wyld Hunt dealing with the problem in session 5, 6, and 7? What if the players call them/mislead them? Which Houses come? What if my player is part of that House? If the Wyld Hunt is there, why aren't they dealing with the Fae Crusade? Are they holding the line? What if we maneuver them to siege the castle? Do you have a plan for that? What if we botch our diplomacy with them and they declare war on us before we can get to the castle and were delayed, to the Fae attack Creation?<br /> <br /> I'll stop there, but do you see the order of magnitude more work it is to deal with every eventuality? I really dont think this is going to go well when you have to wrote this. Its a common complaint that DnD adventures in the Forgotten Realms don't make sense because Drizzt/Elminster/Whoever should be there to stop them before you do. Exalted is a much more interwoven place than The Realms with many powers, can you account for that or are they handwaved away? <br /> <br /> Oh and the Socialite in 6 is a single point of failure. What happens of they die, do we just lose? Do we wait for the Baloran Crusade 2: Electric Boogaloo to begin and then find the castle? Do any Deathlords, Elder Lunars, Great Houses, or Infernal Cults capitalize on that failure? <br /> <br /> These are all questions we answer (probably subconsciously) on the fly as STs. Are you going to answer all of them? If not, where do you draw the line?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 10-19-2020, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T10:17:45-07:00","id":1419033,"title":"","content":"Fair point on the socialite, that needs a fail forward condition, I\u2019ll try to think one up.<br /> <br /> A lot of the other stuff though feels like flandarizarion of Solar power. An investigation Supernal can do amazing things, but they can\u2019t visit the site of a book burning 500 years later and tell you the exact contents of every book burned there. Some stuff you just don\u2019t and can\u2019t know, which is why the ST has veto power on introducing facts and what knowledge a character background gives you access to. Also solar mind control isn\u2019t really a thing, not anymore at least. You can\u2019t just roll 30 successes and make the fairy king your slave, especially if he\u2019s currently trying to kill you and has powerful intimacies supporting his actions. In all other cases you just set things up so that the way forward IS through the Solars manipulating the NPCs into getting what they want. Any NPC who is in a position to be captured by the PCs just can\u2019t have the kind of information that lets them skip to the end. Even Solar investigation doesn\u2019t let you say \u201cthis rumour of missing kids sounds weird, I want to roll Int+Investigation to find out who\u2019s ultimately responsible and where they are.\u201d<br /> <br /> I should mention the local DBs and a Wyld Hunt, that\u2019s true, but for all the other big players they won\u2019t be getting involved. This campaign takes place over the course of, what, five days? Is a Realm Legion getting to the far threshold from the Blessed Isle in under a week? I think needless to say the local forces are not equipped to handle this on their own, hence the PCs mattering. Why would I need to pin down reasons for Leviathan not coming to save the day? He\u2019s 3,000 miles away, busy with his own stuff, and probably doesn\u2019t give a crap about this kingdom if he even knows it exists. It\u2019s a crusade to destroy this kingdom, not Creation. If the Crusade continues on to the rest of the world that\u2019s something you could continue on your own, but for the purposes of this campaign it\u2019s a fail state, you failed to prevent the deaths of hundreds of thousands of people, and the corruption/annihilation of their home.<br /> <br /> As for fey in the party, not really accounting for that, and I don\u2019t think it\u2019s reasonable to expect to. If this was a Wyld Hunt campaign it\u2019s unreasonable to expect it to work with a party of 100% anathema. If your party is all fey and they want to destroy Creation this just isn\u2019t the adventure for you. It\u2019s not all things to all people it\u2019s just AN adventure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T00:36:49-07:00","id":1419530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1418390-exalted-written-campaign?p=1419033#post1419033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for fey in the party, not really accounting for that, and <b>I don\u2019t think it\u2019s reasonable to expect to</b>. If this was a Wyld Hunt campaign it\u2019s unreasonable to expect it to work with a party of 100% anathema. If your party is all fey and they want to destroy Creation this just isn\u2019t the adventure for you. It\u2019s not all things to all people it\u2019s just AN adventure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that it matters, but the two Fair Folk in my party are Allies of the Zenith who converted them to her cause. I highlighted your quote about unreasonable expectations because, surprisingly, I 100% agree with you. It is ureasonable to expect that a Circle is gonna have two Cataphracts on the team. However, I expect that every Circle is gonna have their own &quot;Unreasonable Expectation&quot; that simply can't be accounted for. <br /> <br /> I didn't see a passage that specifically tied this adventure to Threshold, so I'm sorry if I missed that. You said about session 5 <i>&quot;Also the surrounding countryside is being ravaged by the Fey. All over for a hundred miles it seems people are being taken and killed, and monsters roam freely&quot;.</i> This makes me think the Wyld Hunt is getting involved, or at least their local affiliates are. And depending on where this is, id expect it to piss off at least one Deathlord/Elder Lunar/Realm Patriarch. But its not a huge stretch to assume it's out of anyone's backyard so ok. I'll concede that one. <br /> <br /> I dont think the rebuttal to my problem about the Investigator really tracks. Sure, its probably beyond even the abilities of a Solar to use Evidence Restoring Method to fix a centuries destroyed book but\u2026 look man theres a whole session investigation there and the path it leads to is &quot;you fail&quot;. I'd feel pretty bad about heavy Investigate investment if that happened to me. <br /> <br /> This is a good adventure outline, I like it. I'd play it. It has mystery, travel, action, socialize, research, and a big setpiece. I just don't think the format of Exalted lends itself well to the granularity of a published adventure, due to the sheer breadth of unreasonable expectations of options players can have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}